// Non-vacuous `since` with a PAST anchor and a current-request correlation on
// the left — a temporal engine divergence distinct from the `0875` current-anchor
// vacuity case.
//
// The formula is `(A && C) since within 1h B` where
//   A = Transfer{ input.user: context.input.user }   (correlate on the request)
//   C = context.input.amount >= 10                   (a rigid request filter)
//   B = Transfer{ input.user: "carol" }              (the literal anchor)
//
// `0875` exercises the case where the CURRENT event is itself the anchor, so
// the left is checked over the empty range `(i, i]` and is vacuously true
// (the §5.3 `((A S B) ∧ C) ∨ B` rewrite handles that, and `0875` passes the temporal engine).
//
// THIS case exercises the complementary shape: the anchor B is strictly in the
// PAST (a prior `carol` Transfer), and the left `(A && C)` is checked over a
// NON-empty range up to the current step, where A correlates on
// `context.input.user` of the *current* request. The interpreter evaluates
// this correctly (see expected_1.out); the temporal engine compiler returns the wrong
// verdict at the decision step (it denies where the interpreter permits).
//
// Interpreter (oracle) verdicts are correct — this lives in the Passing corpus
// for the interpreter and is a KNOWN temporal engine verdict divergence surfaced by the
// SMT differential fuzzer (dogwood-fuzz-smt). Tracked for the temporal-compiler
// `since` left-guard past-anchor compilation; see the compiler root-cause note.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
        && context.input.amount >= 10)
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
